# infra/

Mox-owned infrastructure definitions (deployment, desired-state reconcilers,
server provisioning). The customer VPS is untrusted (Architecture Rule 3);
all external side effects must be idempotent and audited via
`DesiredState`/`OperationRecord`.

## CapRover

CapRover git deploys look for `captain-definition` at the **repository
root** (not under `infra/`). That file points at `./Dockerfile`, which
builds the web SPA and runs the control plane on port 80.

Required app environment variables:

- `DATABASE_URL` — PostgreSQL
- `MOX_PUBLIC_URL` — public `https://` URL of this app
- `MOX_RUNTIME_MODE=full`
- `MOX_RUNTIME_COMMAND` — production Mox Runtime launch command

Optional: `MOX_SETUP_TOKEN`, `MOX_CORS_ORIGINS`, `MOX_SKIP_MIGRATIONS=1`.
`PORT` and `MOX_WEB_DIST_DIR` are set by the image.